WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.917
By the end of this module, you should be able to build a cleaning workflow rather than a one-off fix.

00:00:04.917 --> 00:00:11.817
You should be able to profile quality problems, normalize representation, validate rules, identify duplicates,

00:00:11.817 --> 00:00:14.492
and use safer SQL patterns for changes.

00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:19.362
You should also be able to explain what your cleaning logic knows and what it does not know.

00:00:19.362 --> 00:00:22.767
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:27.372
a customer master-data project cleaning duplicate profiles.

00:00:27.372 --> 00:00:31.812
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:31.812 --> 00:00:34.837
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:34.837 --> 00:00:40.942
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to defend later:

00:00:40.942 --> 00:00:43.927
what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:43.927 --> 00:00:47.520
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
